From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shelley Vohr <shelley.vohr@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Jun 2019 13:59:37 -0700
Subject: printing.patch

Lets //chrome/browser/printing run against a BrowserContext that is not a
Profile and without enterprise content analysis, and lets the native print
dialog open prefilled with settings the embedder resolved beforehand.

chrome/browser/printing/print_job.cc
chrome/browser/printing/print_view_manager_base.cc
  Look printing prefs up through user_prefs::UserPrefs instead of
  Profile::FromBrowserContext, so an embedder that attaches a PrefService to
  its BrowserContext can use these classes unmodified. Candidate for
  upstreaming.

chrome/browser/printing/print_view_manager_base.cc / .h
  Compile out the enterprise content-analysis hooks. The buildflag cannot be
  turned off from args.gn because Chrome test targets that GN always resolves
  depend on the connectors targets it gates.

chrome/browser/printing/printer_query_oop.cc
  webContents.print(options) resolves its settings with
  PrinterQuery::SetSettings() and then shows the system dialog on the same
  query. With out-of-process printing that query already holds a print
  document client and its settings were applied in the print backend
  service, so keep that client when no UI client id was assigned, and push
  the resolved settings into the in-browser PrintingContext before showing
  the dialog so it opens prefilled (falling back to defaults if the driver
  rejects them). Also release the print document client when a query is
  destroyed without reaching a PrintJob (dialog cancelled, settings
  rejected); upstream leaks it the same way. Candidate for upstreaming.

components/printing/common/print.mojom
components/printing/renderer/print_render_frame_helper.cc
  Report the document's page count in PrintWithParams()'s result. The
  browser needs it to spool the rendered document to a printer, and this
  path does not send DidGetPrintedPagesCount(). Candidate for upstreaming.

